[4] defect D = (F rho) grad U_F - F[rho grad U_F] (matter in hydrostatic equilibrium in the record metric U_F)
    subtraction: none (D measured against zero; ratio to |rho grad U_F|)
    l/R = 0.30: ||D|| / ||rho grad U|| = 1.0102e-01 ; /(l/R)^2 = 1.1225
    l/R = 0.10: ||D|| / ||rho grad U|| = 1.3724e-02 ; /(l/R)^2 = 1.3724
    l/R = 0.03: ||D|| / ||rho grad U|| = 1.2766e-03 ; /(l/R)^2 = 1.4184
    => D != 0 at O(G): R16-14's 'Bianchi holds at O(G^2) because F commutes with d' needs a conserved total source, which literal N lacks

[5] homogeneous static Gaussian noise potential U_n on a periodic box; rho_n = -lap U_n/(4 pi); u1 = <|grad U|^2>/(8 pi)
    subtraction: none (means of positive/indefinite quadratic forms; <rho_n> = 0 exactly)
    <U rho>/u1 over 4 realisations: [2. 2. 2. 2.] (identity: 2)
    insertion (1 + 0.00 U) rho_n: <tau00>/u1 = -7.00, <tau00 + tau_kk>/u1 = -8.00
    insertion (1 + 3.50 U) rho_n: <tau00>/u1 = +0.00, <tau00 + tau_kk>/u1 = -1.00
    insertion (1 + 3.75 U) rho_n: <tau00>/u1 = +0.50, <tau00 + tau_kk>/u1 = -0.50
    insertion (1 + 4.00 U) rho_n: <tau00>/u1 = +1.00, <tau00 + tau_kk>/u1 = +0.00
    insertion (1 + 6.00 U) rho_n: <tau00>/u1 = +5.00, <tau00 + tau_kk>/u1 = +4.00
    (a = 0: meter measures (-g)T, noise added after; a = 4: record multiplied by (-g) classically; a = 6: noise as static dust (-g)u0u0)
    min over a of max(|2a-7|, |2a-8|) = 0.5 at a = 3.75: no one-parameter insertion removes both the energy and the active density
    lapse equation (spatial-gauge invariant): a = 0 (a' = -6): <rho_act> = <lap N2>/(4 pi) = -8.0000 u1 ; harmonic-LL value 2a-8 = -8
    lapse equation (spatial-gauge invariant): a = 4 (a' = -2): <rho_act> = <lap N2>/(4 pi) = -0.0000 u1 ; harmonic-LL value 2a-8 = +0
    lapse equation (spatial-gauge invariant): a = 6 (a' = +0): <rho_act> = <lap N2>/(4 pi) = +4.0000 u1 ; harmonic-LL value 2a-8 = +4
    => the static active density (2a-8)u1 is not a harmonic-gauge artefact; a = 4 (unchanged meter; tau = (-g)(J + t_LL) + t_H formed classically) gives 0

[6] per frame mode: harmonic-gauge h00 is a resonant oscillator driven by the S noise; Poisson-gauge Phi is instantaneous
    subtraction: none.  R(k) = secular harmonic 'energy' / stationary Poisson analogue = (1/2) W^2 |F_t(W)|^2 T tau / I, I = tau int |F_t|^2 dw/2pi
    I = tau int |F_t|^2 dw/(2 pi) = 0.65625 (repaired gain)
    T =   200: E(T) numeric = 106.2031 ; (1/2)|F_t(W)|^2 T = 106.2500
    T =   800: E(T) numeric = 424.9531 ; (1/2)|F_t(W)|^2 T = 425.0000
    strict tau=l/c, l=5e-6    : max_k R(k) at t_H = 2.22e+31 (at k = 1.93e+05 /m)
    strict, l=4e-10           : max_k R(k) at t_H = 2.77e+35 (at k = 2.41e+09 /m)
    tau_c ceiling, l=5e-6     : max_k R(k) at t_H = 7.44e+28 (at k = 6.57e+02 /m)
    => in harmonic gauge the realised S/V record noise carries secular pure-gauge parts ~1e29 x the Poisson-gauge field;
       the LL pseudotensor of the realised field is gauge-dependent, so N must be posed in the frame's Poisson gauge (P-r15b)

[7] qubit toy, 6 steps: weak sigma_z measurement with record-dependent strength eps(q), feedback exp(-i th(q) sigma_x),
    q updated NONLINEARLY from records (q <- q + r + 0.7 r q^2).  Averaged map's Choi matrix; mean-field variant uses <sigma_z>_rho
    record-controlled map: Choi eigenvalues [0.1647 0.1906 0.7574 0.8873] (all >= 0 -> CP) ; trace-preservation err 2.2e-16
    meanfield=False: linearity defect |Phi(mix) - mix(Phi)| = 1.110e-16
    meanfield=True: linearity defect |Phi(mix) - mix(Phi)| = 1.617e-02
    => record-controlled nonlinear feedback is a CP instrument (linear in rho); mean-metric (N-bar-type) feedback is not linear in rho

